      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sabinal was originally called Hammer’s Station and first appeared on maps in 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://texashillcountry.com/sabinal-texas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the Sabinal River, whose shaded banks offer scenic drives and a glimpse of Texas Hill Country heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visituvaldecounty.com/communities/sabinal/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every March, Sabinal hosts the Wild Hog Festival, a local celebration that draws thousands of visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://texashillcountry.com/sabinal-texas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In June, the Cypress Day Celebration marks the blooming of cypress trees and is a staple of Sabinal’s summer calendar.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://texashillcountry.com/sabinal-texas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Badland Texas Rangers provide living history reenactments that educate and entertain crowds in Sabinal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://texashillcountry.com/sabinal-texas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A museum in Sabinal houses fossils and minerals from the Sabinal River Canyon and also features a World War II exhibit.",
